    "1/1": "### Step 1: Bug Scenario Images and Reasoning\n\n**Bug Scenario Images Description:**\n- The first image shows a group of radio buttons with a screen reader output at the bottom. The output reads:  \n  \"Radio button label, selected , radio button, 1 of 6\"\n- The second image shows another group of radio buttons with a screen reader output:  \n  \"selected , radio button, 1 of 3\"\n- The bug report and images indicate that the screen reader is not reading the radio button label in the React version, but it does in the vanilla HTML version.\n\n**Root Cause Reasoning:**\n- The vanilla HTML version uses a `<label for=\"...\">` with the label text inside a `<span class=\"bx--radio-button__label-text\">`.\n- The React version adds an unnecessary `aria-label={labelText}` to the `<label>`, and the label text is not in a dedicated class or structure.\n- According to accessibility best practices, the `<label>` element's text content should be used for screen readers, and `aria-label` should only be used if the label text is not visible or present in the DOM.\n- Adding `aria-label` to the `<label>` can override or confuse screen readers, causing them to skip the actual label text.\n\n### Step 2: Bug Code Snippet Analysis\n\n**File:** `packages/react/src/components/RadioButton/RadioButton.js`\n- The `<label>` element is rendered as:\n  ```jsx\n  <label\n    htmlFor={this.uid}\n    className={`${prefix}--radio-button__label`}\n    aria-label={labelText}>\n    <span className={`${prefix}--radio-button__appearance`} />\n    <span className={innerLabelClasses}>{labelText}</span>\n  </label>\n  ```\n- The problematic part is `aria-label={labelText}` on the `<label>`. This is unnecessary and causes the accessibility issue.\n\n### Step 3: Generate Patch\n\n**Fix:**  \n- Remove the `aria-label={labelText}` from the `<label>` element.\n\n```javascript\n### packages/react/src/components/RadioButton/RadioButton.js\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n        <label\n          htmlFor={this.uid}\n          className={`${prefix}--radio-button__label`}\n          aria-label={labelText}>\n          <span className={`${prefix}--radio-button__appearance`} />\n          <span className={innerLabelClasses}>{labelText}</span>\n        </label>\n=======\n        <label\n          htmlFor={this.uid}\n          className={`${prefix}--radio-button__label`}>\n          <span className={`${prefix}--radio-button__appearance`} />\n          <span className={innerLabelClasses}>{labelText}</span>\n        </label>\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \n- The bug is caused by the unnecessary use of `aria-label` on the `<label>` element, which interferes with screen readers.  \n- The patch removes `aria-label={labelText}` from the `<label>`, restoring correct screen reader behavior."
